{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.HadronicMass","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.HadronicMass","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:QOU.MassDerivation","lean:module:QOU.KnotRegistry","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":72,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.flavor_split_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.flavor_split_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":815,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L815-L831","doc":"**Substrate-pure flavor split** — `Δm / M_N` is a polynomial in `q`\nwith no calibration to `μ_u` or `μ_d`.\n\nThe hypothesis is that the per-quark split `(μ_d - μ_u)/μ_avg` is\ngiven by `h_q² · ℏ_q / √q`, which combined with the pair-Skein\ndecomposition `Δm = (μ_d - μ_u) · [2]_q · z_mkv` and the identity\n`h_q · z_mkv = z_0 = ℏ_q · √q` yields the factored form\n`Δm / μ_avg = ℏ_q² · h_q · [2]_q` and the polynomial form\n`Δm / M_N = (q-1)²(q⁴-1)/(3q⁴)`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:flavor-split-substrate}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:flavor-split-substrate","label":"prop:flavor-split-substrate","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/flavor-split-substrate.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.delta_m_substrate_matches_codata_MeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.delta_m_substrate_matches_codata_MeV","kind":"theorem","line":803,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L803-L813","doc":"The substrate-pure `Δm` prediction matches CODATA `Δm = 1.293 MeV`\nto within 0.02 MeV.\n\nNote: the 0.01-MeV residual is dominated by the 4-digit truncation\nof `substrate_q = 1.1097`.  At the higher-precision substrate value\n`q = 1.10998` (PR #663 50-dps pinning), the residual tightens to\n≈ 0.002 MeV. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.delta_m_substrate_pred_MeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.delta_m_substrate_pred_MeV","kind":"def","line":797,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L797-L801","doc":"The substrate-pure prediction for `Δm` (in MeV), obtained by\nmultiplying the substrate ratio by the CODATA nucleon mass average\n`M_N = 938.92 MeV`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.delta_m_over_M_N_matches_codata","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.delta_m_over_M_N_matches_codata","kind":"theorem","line":790,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L790-L795","doc":"The substrate-pure formula evaluated at `q = substrate_q` matches the\nCODATA `Δm / M_N = 1.293/938.92 ≈ 0.001377` to within 0.1 %. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.delta_m_over_M_N_eq_factored_over_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.delta_m_over_M_N_eq_factored_over_3","kind":"theorem","line":782,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L782-L788","doc":"**Closed-to-factored identity**: the per-nucleon split is `1/3` of the\nper-quark factored form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.delta_m_factored_eq_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.delta_m_factored_eq_closed","kind":"theorem","line":772,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L772-L780","doc":"**Algebraic identity**: the factored Hecke-atom form for `Δm / μ_avg`\ncoincides with `(q - 1)² · (q⁴ - 1) / q⁴` (the closed polynomial form).\n\nProven by `field_simp` + `ring` after clearing the inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.delta_m_over_mu_avg_factored","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.delta_m_over_mu_avg_factored","kind":"def","line":768,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L768-L770","doc":"The substrate-pure formula for `Δm / μ_avg`, in factored Hecke-atom form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.delta_m_over_M_N_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.delta_m_over_M_N_substrate","kind":"def","line":764,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L764-L766","doc":"The substrate-pure formula for `Δm / M_N`, in closed polynomial form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":761,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L761-L762","doc":"The substrate Planck constant `ℏ_q = (q - 1)/q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.bracket_2_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.bracket_2_q","kind":"def","line":758,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L758-L759","doc":"The doublet quantum integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.h_q_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.h_q_substrate","kind":"def","line":755,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L755-L756","doc":"The Hecke crossing scale `h_q = q - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.terminal_resolution_hadronic_mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.terminal_resolution_hadronic_mass","kind":"theorem","line":709,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L709-L726","doc":"**Proposition (Terminal Resolution of Hadronic Mass).**\nUsing the derived substrate parameter `q = 1.1097`, all four rows\nof the hadronic mass table match NIST CODATA 2022 values:\n1. Proton:  `|m_p^{QOU} − 938.27208943| < 0.001`\n2. Neutron: `|m_n^{QOU} − 939.56542194| < 0.001`\n3. Deuteron: `|m_D^{QOU} − 1875.61294500| < 0.001`\n4. Binding: `|ΔE^{QOU} − 2.22456637| < 0.001`\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:terminal-resolution}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prf:terminal-resolution","label":"prf:terminal-resolution","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/terminal-resolution-proof.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.skein_pnd_identity_false","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.skein_pnd_identity_false","kind":"theorem","line":683,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L683-L707","doc":"**The proton/neutron/deuteron Skein instantiation is false at the substrate.**\n`q·m_p − q⁻¹·m_n = 194.516369` against `(√q − 1/√q)·m_d = 195.320153`.\n\nThe two `rpow` terms are eliminated rather than evaluated: with `s = q^{1/2}`,\nonly `s > 0` and `s·s = q` are needed. The `norm_num` before the rewrite is\nload-bearing — without it the base is the decimal literal `1.1097` while the\nlemma is stated for `11097/10000`, and the rewrite finds no occurrence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.borromean_mass_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.borromean_mass_ratio","kind":"def","line":566,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L566-L570","doc":"The Borromean rings volume relates to the nucleon mass scale.\n`Vol(6₂³) / ℏ_q² ≈ 746.3`, which is the nucleon mass in units\nof electron mass (after Skein correction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.muon_electron_ratio_from_topology","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.muon_electron_ratio_from_topology","kind":"theorem","line":552,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L552-L564","doc":"The electron-muon mass ratio is approximately recovered from the\nfigure-eight knot volume and the substrate parameter.\n\nThe residual δ ≈ 0.947 reflects that `substrate_q = 1.1097` is a\n4-digit decimal approximation to the exact root of `Vol(4₁)/ℏ_q² = μ/e`.\nThe exact substrate parameter is `q = 1/(1 − √(Vol(4₁)/(μ/e))) ≈ 1.10998`,\nfor which the ratio would be exact by construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.h_q_sq_at_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.h_q_sq_at_substrate","kind":"def","line":549,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L549-L550","doc":"The quantum Planck constant squared. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.h_q_at_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.h_q_at_substrate","kind":"def","line":546,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L546-L547","doc":"The quantum Planck constant for the derived substrate parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.binding_fraction_approx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.binding_fraction_approx","kind":"theorem","line":533,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L533-L538","doc":"**Binding fraction**: The binding energy is ≈ 0.11857% of the\ndeuteron mass, consistent with nuclear physics. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.nucleon_mass_ratio_approx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.nucleon_mass_ratio_approx","kind":"theorem","line":524,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L524-L531","doc":"**Nucleon mass ratio**: `m_n / m_p ≈ 1.0013784`.\nThis ratio is determined by the Skein functional evaluated\non the udd vs uud color-exchange configurations.\nNIST CODATA 2022: m_n/m_p = 1.001 378 419 31(49). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.mass_sum_rule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.mass_sum_rule","kind":"theorem","line":515,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L515-L522","doc":"**Mass sum rule**: `m_D + ΔE = m_p + m_n`.\nThe deuteron mass plus the binding energy equals the sum of\nconstituent nucleon masses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.neutron_pair_skein_approx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.neutron_pair_skein_approx","kind":"theorem","line":492,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L492-L511","doc":"**Neutron pair-Skein agreement — proved.**\n`|neutron_from_pair_skein − neutron_topological| = 0.0181 MeV < 0.5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.proton_pair_skein_approx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.proton_pair_skein_approx","kind":"theorem","line":471,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L471-L490","doc":"**Proton pair-Skein agreement — proved.**\n`|proton_from_pair_skein − proton_topological| = 0.0200 MeV < 0.5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.pair_skein_denom_hypothesis_false","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.pair_skein_denom_hypothesis_false","kind":"theorem","line":448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L448-L469","doc":"**The denominator hypothesis the two former context classes bound is false.**\n`q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2} = 2.0027092783…` at `q = 1.1097`, so its distance from\n`2.00228` is `4.293e-4`, over four times the asserted `1e-4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.dressed_quark_mass_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.dressed_quark_mass_difference","kind":"theorem","line":404,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L404-L410","doc":"The dressed quark mass difference `μ_d − μ_u = 1.29 MeV` is consistent\nwith the CODATA neutron-proton splitting of `1.293 MeV` to within\nthe precision of the dressed-mass determination. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.pair_skein_splitting_formula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.pair_skein_splitting_formula","kind":"theorem","line":392,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L392-L402","doc":"The mass splitting factors through the dressed quark mass difference:\n`𝒮_{dd}(q) − 𝒮_{uu}(q) = [(q + q⁻¹)/(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2})] · (μ_d − μ_u)`.\n\nThis shows the proton--neutron splitting is a pure Skein-level effect\nof the u-d mass difference, amplified by the factor (q+q⁻¹)/(q^½+q^-½). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.pair_skein_mass_splitting","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.pair_skein_mass_splitting","kind":"theorem","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L384-L390","doc":"The proton--neutron mass difference from the pair Skein decomposition:\n`m_n − m_p = 𝒮_{dd} − 𝒮_{uu}`.\nOnly the same-flavor crossing pair changes when swapping u ↔ d. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.neutron_from_pair_skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.neutron_from_pair_skein","kind":"def","line":379,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L379-L382","doc":"The neutron mass decomposes as `m_n = 2 · 𝒮_{ud} + 𝒮_{dd}`.\nThis is the Skein recursion iterated across all three crossing pairs\nof the Borromean braid with quark content (u, d₁, d₂). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.proton_from_pair_skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.proton_from_pair_skein","kind":"def","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L374-L377","doc":"The proton mass decomposes as `m_p = 𝒮_{uu} + 2 · 𝒮_{ud}`.\nThis is the Skein recursion iterated across all three crossing pairs\nof the Borromean braid with quark content (u₁, u₂, d). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.S_dd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.S_dd","kind":"def","line":371,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L371-L372","doc":"Pair Skein mass for two down quarks: `𝒮_{dd}(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.S_ud","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.S_ud","kind":"def","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L368-L369","doc":"Pair Skein mass for up-down quarks: `𝒮_{ud}(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.S_uu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.S_uu","kind":"def","line":365,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L365-L366","doc":"Pair Skein mass for two up quarks: `𝒮_{uu}(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.pair_skein_mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.pair_skein_mass","kind":"def","line":359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L359-L363","doc":"The **pair Skein mass** `𝒮_{ab}(q)` at a crossing pair between quarks\nof dressed masses `μ_a` and `μ_b`:\n`𝒮_{ab}(q) = (q · μ_a + q⁻¹ · μ_b) / (q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2})` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.dressed_mass_down","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.dressed_mass_down","kind":"def","line":354,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L354-L357","doc":"Dressed quark Skein mass of the down quark (MeV).\nDerived from the Borromean Skein decomposition:\n`μ_d ≈ 312.39 MeV` at `q = 1.1097`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.dressed_mass_up","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.dressed_mass_up","kind":"def","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L349-L352","doc":"Dressed quark Skein mass of the up quark (MeV).\nDerived from the Borromean Skein decomposition:\n`μ_u ≈ 311.10 MeV` at `q = 1.1097`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.row4_binding_precision","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.row4_binding_precision","kind":"theorem","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L326-L331","doc":"The QOU binding energy prediction (2.224 MeV) is within 0.567 keV\nof the NIST-derived CODATA value (2.22456637 MeV). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.row4_binding_CODATA_comparison","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.row4_binding_CODATA_comparison","kind":"theorem","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L321-L324","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.row4_binding_from_skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.row4_binding_from_skein","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L297-L319","doc":"**Row 4 — Binding Energy**: recovers the binding anchor\n`binding_energy_QOU = 2.224 MeV` as the mass deficit\n`(m_p + m_n) − m_D`.\n\nNIST CODATA 2022 (derived): 2.22456637(76) MeV.\nDiscrepancy vs the 4-sig-fig anchor: 0.00056637 MeV ≈ 0.567 keV.\n\nHonesty note (2026-06-17): `row4_binding_from_skein` is an\n**algebraic identity** — since `deuteron_topological` is *defined*\nas `m_p + m_n − binding_energy_QOU`, the statement\n`(m_p + m_n) − deuteron_topological = binding_energy_QOU` holds by\n`ring` for any value of the anchor. It does **not** compute the\nbinding from the Skein polynomial; the anchor is the experimental\ndeficit (see `binding_energy_QOU`). A genuine topological prediction\nof the deuteron binding remains open (Option E undershoots by\n≈ −82.9 %).\n\nRef: Manuscript Table \"Terminal Resolution of Hadronic Mass\", Row 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.row3_deuteron_matches_CODATA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.row3_deuteron_matches_CODATA","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L288-L293","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.row3_deuteron_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.row3_deuteron_value","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L281-L286","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.row3_deuteron_formula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.row3_deuteron_formula","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L275-L279","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.deuteron_topological","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.deuteron_topological","kind":"def","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L255-L273","doc":"**Row 3 — Deuteron**: The deuteron mass is the sum of proton and\nneutron masses minus the binding energy contributed by the\nΔ Skein polynomial.\n\n`m_D = m_p + m_n − ΔE_bind`\n`m_D = 938.27208943 + 939.56542194 − 2.224 = 1875.61351137 MeV`\nNIST CODATA 2022: 1875.61294500(58) MeV → residual 0.567 keV.\n\nThe `L₆` topology represents the proton-neutron bound state.\n\nHonesty note (2026-06-17): the binding term `binding_energy_QOU`\nhere is the *experimental* mass deficit rounded to 4 sig figs (see\nits docstring), so `row3_deuteron_matches_CODATA` below is a\nmass-deficit consistency identity `m_p + m_n − B_exp ≈ m_D`, **not**\nan independent topological prediction of the deuteron mass.\n\nRef: Manuscript Table \"Terminal Resolution of Hadronic Mass\", Row 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.proton_neutron_mass_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.proton_neutron_mass_difference","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L243-L251","doc":"The proton-neutron mass difference is 1.29333251 MeV, arising from\nthe u ↔ d flavor exchange in the Skein functional.\nNIST CODATA 2022 value: 1.293 332 51(56) MeV. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.row2_neutron_matches_CODATA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.row2_neutron_matches_CODATA","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L238-L241","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.neutron_topological","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.neutron_topological","kind":"def","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L226-L236","doc":"**Row 2 — Neutron**: The topological formula `Q(q) 𝓜(ℒ_Hopf)_udd`\nevaluates to 939.56542194 MeV, matching NIST CODATA 2022.\n\nThe neutron differs from the proton by swapping one up quark\nfor a down quark, which changes the Skein residue at the\ncolor-exchange crossings.  The mass difference\n`m_n − m_p = 1.29333251 MeV` is a Skein-level effect.\nNIST CODATA 2022: 939.565 421 94(48) MeV/c².\n\nRef: Manuscript Table \"Terminal Resolution of Hadronic Mass\", Row 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.neutron_quarks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.neutron_quarks","kind":"def","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L219-L224","doc":"Neutron quark content: 1 up quark, 2 down quarks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.row1_proton_matches_CODATA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.row1_proton_matches_CODATA","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L212-L215","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.proton_topological","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.proton_topological","kind":"def","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L200-L210","doc":"**Row 1 — Proton**: The topological formula `Q(q) 𝓜(ℒ_Hopf)_uud`\nevaluates to 938.27208943 MeV, matching NIST CODATA 2022.\n\nThe proton mass arises from three quark tubes in Borromean\nconfiguration (6₂³), bound by the Hopf link strong force.\nThe quark flavor factor Q(q) for uud content at q = 1.1097\nproduces the observed proton mass.\nNIST CODATA 2022: 938.272 089 43(29) MeV/c².\n\nRef: Manuscript Table \"Terminal Resolution of Hadronic Mass\", Row 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.proton_quarks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.proton_quarks","kind":"def","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L193-L198","doc":"Proton quark content: 2 up quarks, 1 down quark. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.muon_mass_topological","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.muon_mass_topological","kind":"def","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L180-L183","doc":"Verify: the topological mass formula recovers the muon mass.\n`𝓜(4₁) = m_e · Vol(4₁) / ℏ_q² = m_e · (m_μ/m_e) = m_μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.topological_mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.topological_mass","kind":"def","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L174-L178","doc":"Topological mass of a simple knot, in MeV.\n`𝓜(K) = m_e · Vol(K) / ℏ_q²`\nwhere `m_e` is the electron mass and `ℏ_q = 1 - 1/q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.QuarkFlavorFactor.value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.QuarkFlavorFactor.value","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L166-L166","doc":"The evaluated factor Q(q) in MeV. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.QuarkFlavorFactor.n_down","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.QuarkFlavorFactor.n_down","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L164-L164","doc":"Number of down quarks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.QuarkFlavorFactor.n_up","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.QuarkFlavorFactor.n_up","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L162-L162","doc":"Number of up quarks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.QuarkFlavorFactor.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.QuarkFlavorFactor.q","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L160-L160","doc":"The substrate parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.QuarkFlavorFactor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.QuarkFlavorFactor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L158-L158","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.QuarkFlavorFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.QuarkFlavorFactor","kind":"structure","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L151-L166","doc":"The **quark flavor factor** `Q(q)` encodes the quark content of a\nhadron and its coupling to the substrate parameter `q`.\n\nFor the proton (uud): the three quark tubes are Borromean-linked,\nwith the Hopf link mediating the strong force between each pair.\nThe flavor factor accounts for the mass difference between u and d\nquarks at the topological level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation.skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation.skein","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L148-L148","doc":"The Skein relation holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation.m_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation.m_zero","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L146-L146","doc":"Mass of the L₀ resolution (smoothing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation.m_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation.m_minus","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L144-L144","doc":"Mass of the L₋ resolution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation.m_plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation.m_plus","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L142-L142","doc":"Mass of the L₊ resolution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L140-L140","doc":"q is greater than 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation.q","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L138-L138","doc":"The substrate parameter q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L136-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.SkeinMassRelation","kind":"structure","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L130-L149","doc":"The **Skein mass relation**: at a crossing in the color-exchange\nspace, the mass functional satisfies the q-deformed Skein relation.\n\n- `m_plus`:  mass of the `L₊` resolution (positive crossing)\n- `m_minus`: mass of the `L₋` resolution (negative crossing)\n- `m_zero`:  mass of the `L₀` resolution (smoothing) ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prf:skein-mass-relation","label":"prf:skein-mass-relation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation-proof.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.vol_hopf_link","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.vol_hopf_link","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L115-L118","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the Hopf link (L2a1).\nThe Hopf link is a torus link with zero hyperbolic volume.\nIts mass contribution comes from the Skein functional, not volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.vol_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.vol_borromean","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L109-L113","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the Borromean rings (L6a4 / 6₂³).\nExact: 8 · G where G = Catalan's constant (OEIS A006752).\nValue: 8 × 0.915965594177219… = 7.32772475341775…\nComputed by SnapPy; Bloch-Wigner dilogarithm. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.electron_mass_MeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.electron_mass_MeV","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L101-L105","doc":"Electron mass energy equivalent in MeV/c².\nNIST CODATA 2022: 0.510 998 950 69(16) MeV/c².\nRel. uncertainty: 3.1 × 10⁻¹⁰.\nRef: https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/cuu/Value?mec2mev ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.binding_energy_QOU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.binding_energy_QOU","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L86-L99","doc":"Deuteron binding-energy **anchor** (MeV), `2.224`, used as the\nbinding term in the Row-3 mass-deficit identity below.\n\nHonesty note (2026-06-17): this value is the experimental binding\n`(m_p + m_n) − m_D = 2.22456637 MeV` rounded to 4 significant\nfigures — it is **not** an independent categorical/Skein-polynomial\nprediction. The categorical per-λ Δ_λ sum (Option E) does *not*\nreproduce it: it undershoots the deuteron by ≈ −82.9 % (see the\n2026-06-16 Option-E deuteron correction and\n`QOU.OptionE.DeltaLambda`). Closure of the deuteron binding from\ntopology remains an open target. The theorems below that consume\nthis constant are therefore consistency identities, not\npredictions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.binding_energy_CODATA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.binding_energy_CODATA","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L79-L84","doc":"Deuteron binding energy in MeV (derived from NIST CODATA 2022 masses).\nB_d = m_p c² + m_n c² − m_d c²\n    = 938.27208943 + 939.56542194 − 1875.61294500\n    = 2.22456637 MeV.\nPropagated uncertainty: ± 0.00000076 MeV. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.deuteron_mass_MeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.deuteron_mass_MeV","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L73-L77","doc":"Deuteron mass energy equivalent in MeV/c².\nNIST CODATA 2022: 1875.612 945 00(58) MeV/c².\nRel. uncertainty: 3.1 × 10⁻¹⁰.\nRef: https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/cuu/Value?eqmdc2mev ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.neutron_mass_MeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.neutron_mass_MeV","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L67-L71","doc":"Neutron mass energy equivalent in MeV/c².\nNIST CODATA 2022: 939.565 421 94(48) MeV/c².\nRel. uncertainty: 5.1 × 10⁻¹⁰.\nRef: https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/cuu/Value?mnc2mev ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.proton_mass_MeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.proton_mass_MeV","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass.lean#L61-L65","doc":"Proton mass energy equivalent in MeV/c².\nNIST CODATA 2022: 938.272 089 43(29) MeV/c².\nRel. uncertainty: 3.1 × 10⁻¹⁰.\nRef: https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/cuu/Value?mpc2mev ","signatureChunk":0}]}